## `itd_complete` Function — Transaction Length Handling

Here is the complete function, which processes completed isochronous Transfer Descriptors:

```c
static bool itd_complete(struct ehci_hcd *ehci, struct ehci_itd *itd)
{
	struct urb				*urb = itd->urb;
	struct usb_iso_packet_descriptor	*desc;
	u32					t;
	unsigned				uframe;
	int					urb_index = -1;
	struct ehci_iso_stream			*stream = itd->stream;
	bool					retval = false;

	/* for each uframe with a packet */
	for (uframe = 0; uframe < 8; uframe++) {
		if (likely(itd->index[uframe] == -1))
			continue;
		urb_index = itd->index[uframe];
		desc = &urb->iso_frame_desc[urb_index];

		t = hc32_to_cpup(ehci, &itd->hw_transaction[uframe]);
		itd->hw_transaction[uframe] = 0;

		/* report transfer status */
		if (unlikely(t & ISO_ERRS)) {
			urb->error_count++;
			if (t & EHCI_ISOC_BUF_ERR)
				desc->status = usb_pipein(urb->pipe)
					? -ENOSR  /* hc couldn't read */
					: -ECOMM; /* hc couldn't write */
			else if (t & EHCI_ISOC_BABBLE)
				desc->status = -EOVERFLOW;
			else /* (t & EHCI_ISOC_XACTERR) */
				desc->status = -EPROTO;

			/* HC need not update length with this error */
			if (!(t & EHCI_ISOC_BABBLE)) {
				desc->actual_length = EHCI_ITD_LENGTH(t);
				urb->actual_length += desc->actual_length;
			}
		} else if (likely((t & EHCI_ISOC_ACTIVE) == 0)) {
			desc->status = 0;
			desc->actual_length = EHCI_ITD_LENGTH(t);
			urb->actual_length += desc->actual_length;
		} else {
			/* URB was too late */
			urb->error_count++;
		}
	}

	/* handle completion now? */
	if (likely((urb_index + 1) != urb->number_of_packets))
		goto done;

	/* give urb back to the driver; completion often (re)submits */
	ehci_urb_done(ehci, urb, 0);
	retval = true;
	urb = NULL;

	--ehci->isoc_count;
	disable_periodic(ehci);

	ehci_to_hcd(ehci)->self.bandwidth_isoc_reqs--;
	if (ehci_to_hcd(ehci)->self.bandwidth_isoc_reqs == 0) {
		if (ehci->amd_pll_fix == 1)
			usb_amd_quirk_pll_enable();
	}

	if (unlikely(list_is_singular(&stream->td_list)))
		ehci_to_hcd(ehci)->self.bandwidth_allocated
				-= stream->bandwidth;

done:
	itd->urb = NULL;

	/* Add to the end of the free list for later reuse */
	list_move_tail(&itd->itd_list, &stream->free_list);

	/* Recycle the iTDs when the pipeline is empty (ep no longer in use) */
	if (list_empty(&stream->td_list)) {
		list_splice_tail_init(&stream->free_list,
				&ehci->cached_itd_list);
		start_free_itds(ehci);
	}

	return retval;
}
```

### How the Transaction Length Is Read and Used

The function iterates over all 8 uframe slots within the iTD. For each populated slot, it reads the hardware transaction status word:

```c
t = hc32_to_cpup(ehci, &itd->hw_transaction[uframe]);
```

This `t` value contains both status bits and the transfer length packed together. The length is then extracted via the macro `EHCI_ITD_LENGTH(t)`, which extracts the length from bits 16–27 of the transaction word (the lower 12 bits of the `Length` field, shifted right by 16).

### How `actual_length` Is Calculated

The actual length is assigned directly from the macro extraction in **two** code paths:

1. **Error path (non-babble):** When an error other than babble occurs, `"desc->actual_length = EHCI_ITD_LENGTH(t)"` is set, and it is accumulated into `urb->actual_length`.

2. **Success path:** When the transfer completed normally (active bit is clear and no error bits are set), the same assignment `"desc->actual_length = EHCI_ITD_LENGTH(t)"` applies.

Notably, for babble errors (`EHCI_ISOC_BABBLE`), the actual length is **not** updated — only the status is set to `-EOVERFLOW`.

This is contrasted with how the length was originally written during `itd_patch`, where the length was shifted left by 16 bits: `"trans |= length << 16"`. The `EHCI_ITD_LENGTH` macro essentially reverses this packing to recover the bytes actually transferred.

